Washington State BEAD Program | Washington State Department of Commerce

Washington State BEAD Program

Washington State received $1.2 billion in federal BEAD funding to expand broadband access to unserved and underserved areas. Washington's BEAD Initial Proposal was approved by NTIA on April 30, 2026. The state has officially entered the subgrantee selection process.

Key Dates:
- April 30, 2026: Initial Proposal approved
- May–October 2026: Subgrantee selection process
- Q3 2026: Expected construction start for first subgrantees
- 2030: Deployment deadline

Washington BEAD footprint: ~185,000 unserved locations across 39 counties
Priority areas: Eastern Washington, rural Snohomish County, rural Skagit County, rural Whatcom County

Local engineering firms will be needed to support permitting, survey, and construction inspection across rural corridors.
