Community Fiber Network - Snohomish County PUD
Snohomish County PUD Community Fiber Network

Snohomish County PUD is building a middle-mile and last-mile fiber optic network to serve unserved and underserved communities across Snohomish County.

The PUD is actively working with local ISPs and engineering partners to design and deploy fiber infrastructure. The project involves coordination with state and county permitting agencies.

Key details:
- Service area: Rural Snohomish County
- Technology: FTTH (Fiber to the Home)
- Status: Active design and permitting phase (as of 2025-2026)
- Partners: Working with local engineering and survey firms for field work and design

Permitting challenges: Projects require coordination with WSDOT, county road departments, and various utility districts. Permit review times have varied significantly across jurisdictions.
